# ============================================================================
# FILE:       backend-test/.vercelignore
# PURPOSE:    Controls what Vercel uploads when this folder is deployed as a
#             standalone project (Root Directory = backend-test).
# HOW IT WORKS: Every pattern below removes files from the deployment bundle.
#             Keep `app/`, `api/`, `alembic/`, `requirements.txt` and `.env` —
#             the runtime needs them.
# KEY CONCEPTS: bundle size, cold start time, dependency-free uploads.
# ============================================================================

# --- Local development artefacts -----------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- Not needed at runtime ------------------------------------------------
tests/
logs/
*.log
seed.py
pytest.ini
requirements-dev.txt

# --- Version control / editors -------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
